module v1.compiler.trait_bound_witness

data trait_bound_witness_import_note: String = "This module takes no v1.compiler.emit_rust import deliberately: v1.compiler.emit_rust (src/v1/05_emit_rust.dag) is the consumer that wires v1_fn_body_match_scrutinee_rc_clone_bound_param_names's caller inline (emit_fn_def), and it already owns analyze_rc_match (defined locally) and match_scrutinee/match_arm_nodes/authored_name_at (already imported) -- importing them here as well, while emit_rust.dag imports this module's decision core, would be an import cycle (emit_rust -> trait_bound_witness -> emit_rust), forbidden as the substrate's one structural law (DESIGN.md S4 acyclicity). So this module stays strictly downstream: it owns only the Node-free pure decision core and the union helper; the Node/EmitGraphInfo-consuming extraction step lives at the call site in emit_fn_def instead of a wrapper here."

data trait_bound_witness_note: String = "gunbc dashboard node://adhoc-d30225a0-531 (E0599 cluster in materialization_carriers). Derives, from real compiler operation facts rather than a text scan of emitted Rust (DESIGN.md S5 construction-over-validation), the generic function parameters that need a Clone bound because emit_typed_match's RC-deref-clone lowering (analyze_rc_match/analyze_rc_pattern, both unmodified here) fires on a match whose scrutinee resolves to a shared/Rc-wrapped, generic-parameterized coproduct. Root cause traced to emit_fn_def (src/v1/05_emit_rust.dag): it calls v1_generic_params_needing_clone_bound (src/v1/trait_derive_emit.dag) with value_params/ret/bounds/type_decl_items but never with the function body, so the Clone-bound decision chain is structurally blind to what a function BODY does with a generic-parameterized value -- specifically the .clone() call that lowering emits on the dereferenced pointee, which needs the pointee's generic parameter bound, producing rustc E0599 (no method named `clone` found for type parameter `T`) at the generated call site today. CROSS-LANE GROUNDING: this lowering seam is already censused at dag/tools/e0599_emitter_decision_census.dag under cause CloneSharedRequirement, lowering operation DerefCloneWholeValue (emit_typed_match / emit_rust_tco_match via v1.compiler.languages rust_spec.sharing.deref_clone, 139 counted occurrences at that census's snapshot); that census is diagnostic-only by its own declared scope (e0599_emitter_decision_census_note: 'B0 is explicitly forbidden from pre-committing the sharing carrier') and names the carrier question as open among v2.std.compilers.target_model.RequiredTraitWitness, a capability-keyed contract, or docs/plans/emitter-ownership-defork.md's UseSiteVerdict.CloneShared. NO NEW CARRIER TYPE, AND NOT RequiredTraitWitness (checked, not assumed): RequiredTraitWitness's four consuming functions are all keyed to a specific different question -- whether a chosen Rust COLLECTION REPRESENTATION's element type (BTreeSet/HashSet/Vec, TargetRepresentationChoice.constraints) satisfies Ord/Hash/Eq -- and one of them, target_collection_trait_witness_satisfied (v2.std.compilers.target_model, ~line 10531), matches every witness variant against an `elem: Node` collection-element-kernel-shape check (target_collection_element_ord_eligible / _hash_eligible / _eq_eligible: string/int/bool/unit kernel atoms only). A bare generic function parameter needing Clone because a function body derefs+clones an Rc-wrapped match scrutinee has no `elem` and is not a collection representation choice at all; folding it into RequiredTraitWitness would force a meaningless arm into that elem-eligibility match rather than extend a shared concept (DESIGN.md S3's generalize-on-its-own-authority carve-out does not apply when the existing consumers are provably answering an unrelated question, not merely a narrowly-prefixed one). Given that, and given DESIGN.md S3/S5 forbid landing a second NAMED carrier for one fact, the fix here mints no type at all: the two functions below return plain List<String> param names -- the exact same shape v1_generic_params_needing_clone_bound (the real consumer) already returns and unions today -- so there is nothing to reconcile against a future B1 decision beyond unioning two String lists, and nothing here competes with whichever carrier the sharing lane eventually derives. The decision core (v1_rc_match_scrutinee_clone_bound_param_names) is deliberately pure -- it takes already-extracted facts (generic param names, the scrutinee's resolved type name and type-argument names, and analyze_rc_match's needs_deref verdict) and is unit-testable with plain literals, no Node construction required. The Node-consuming extraction wrapper (v1_fn_body_match_scrutinee_rc_clone_bound_param_names) is the thin layer that calls analyze_rc_match and feeds the pure core; it is wired into emit_fn_def below (05_emit_rust.dag) and scoped narrowly to a function body that IS DIRECTLY a top-level match expression (the exact shape of the two real specimens this was traced from, realize_route<T> and classify_write<T> in dag/std/cache_interface.dag) -- a body wrapped in Let/If/Branch before reaching the match is NOT walked. That is a declared boundary, not a silent gap: BoundedToDirectTopLevelMatchBody names it below, and the next-rung trigger is a recursive body walker mirroring emit_rust_expr_if/emit_rust_expr_let's accessor shapes once a second real specimen needs it (DESIGN.md S4b no-untracked-stall)."

type TraitBoundWitnessScope
  = BoundedToDirectTopLevelMatchBody

fn v1_rc_match_scrutinee_clone_bound_param_names(
  generic_param_names: List<String>,
  scrutinee_type_arg_names: List<String>,
  rc_match_needs_deref: Bool
) -> List<String> {
  if !rc_match_needs_deref {
    []
  } else {
    scrutinee_type_arg_names
    |> flat_map(arg_name =>
      if generic_param_names |> any(g => g == arg_name) {
        [arg_name]
      } else {
        []
      }
    )
  }
}

fn v1_union_clone_param_names(base: List<String>, extra: List<String>) -> List<String> {
  concat(base, extra |> filter(x => !(base |> any(y => y == x))))
}
